# OksaSDR tour, "The app's own": beat cancel (BC) on a real case: a phone QSO tuned onto its
# station ({DIAL} LSB, the dial on its carrier) with a steady carrier inside the 2.9 kHz passband,
# {OFF} kHz below the dial: a whistle over the voice. Receive only; BC put back off.
pin 5
record 15
caption !speed 3
caption # The app's own
ready
wait 4000
caption !speed 1
caption Beat cancel (BC), the app's own, not in SmartSDR. In a phone QSO someone tunes up on your frequency: a steady whistle over the voice, worst in headphones.
freq {DIAL}
span 10
wait 1000
caption !mark 560,115
mode LSB
wait 2000
caption !mark 933,115
popup filterChooser
wait 1500
taptext 2.9k
wait 1500
close
wait 1000
caption A real one on {BAND}: the QSO on {DIAL} MHz with a steady carrier inside the passband, a {HZ} Hz whistle over the voice.
wait 9000
caption Tap the DSP flags, then BC: it finds the steady carrier and notches it out within 0.15 s; the voice stays.
taptext NR ~600,126
wait 2000
taptext BC ~743,464
wait 12000
caption BC off: the whistle is back. Up to four carriers at a time, in the voice modes.
taptext BC ~743,464
wait 6000
close
wait 1000
caption -
record off
freq 14.074
mode DIGU
wait 2000
slices
